Luma for Raspberry Pi 5 (installer: @ISO_NAME@)

This card starts the Luma installer, and after installing, the Luma installed
on NVMe or USB. Keep it in the Pi.

Partition 1 (LUMA_PI5, this one): config.txt, U-Boot, device trees, GRUB and
the installer kernel. Partition 2: the unmodified Luma installer ISO.

The installer on this card may be older than the current Luma release.
Install, then update from Settings; the installed system updates itself.

Choose a different menu entry for the next boot from a running Luma:
  sudo luma-rpi5-boot-next install     (reinstall)
  sudo luma-rpi5-boot-next rescue
The GRUB menu on HDMI cannot be driven with a USB keyboard.
